{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations from `requirements.cli.setup_local_path`: (1) with `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, setup adds that local crate as the dev dependency. (2) Repeating setup does not add a duplicate. (3) The text implies an existing Habeas dev dependency is not duplicated or replaced.\n\nCoverage:\n- (1) `tests/setup.rs#fn[local_path_setup_adds_exactly_that_crate_once]` starts from a fixture manifest with no dependencies and runs `setup --path` with a relative path. It checks that exactly one `habeas` entry exists across the dependencies, dev-dependencies and build-dependencies tables. It checks that the entry is in `dev-dependencies` and that its `path` canonicalizes to the given crate directory. `setup_is_repeatable` also checks that a `path =` dev dependency is written.\n- (2) The same test reruns setup with an absolute path to the same crate and asserts that `Cargo.toml` is byte-identical. `setup_is_repeatable` runs setup twice and checks the manifest still contains the dependency. The first test's count assertion, via `habeas_dependencies`, catches duplicates.\n- (3) `local_path_setup_keeps_an_existing_habeas_dev_dependency` pre-populates `[dev-dependencies] habeas = \"0.1\"`, runs `setup --path`, and asserts that the manifest is unchanged. This covers the \"no existing dependency\" precondition from the other side.\n- `local_path_setup_rejects_a_missing_crate_directory` checks a failure case the text does not name. It is extra and harmless.\n\nThe assertions enforce the expected outcomes, and the helpers `fixture`, `run` and `habeas_dependencies` are sound. I found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "9b8a0a947e27a013ee7462c3718ba69c09b959d8490690a36c55b448e43d7d4d",
